message:
Empty and unknown coupon codes crashed `apply_coupon` with an unhandled `KeyError`; added an explicit guard that raises `ValueError` for blank or unrecognised codes before the dict lookup. Added `tests/test_issue_1.py` covering both `pricing.apply_coupon` and `cart.total()` paths; full suite green (37 passed).
@m13-ops-maint
RESULT
```json
{"status": "proposed", "summary": "Empty coupon code no longer crashes checkout", "evidence": ["tests/test_issue_1.py fails before the fix (KeyError), passes after (ValueError)", "pytest -q: 37 passed", "commit 9b3838f on m13-gen-2-fix-1"], "pr": "m13-gen-2-fix-1"}
```

`price_after_discount_and_tax()` was calling `apply_tax()` internally, so any caller that also applied tax (cart total, checkout receipt) would charge it twice — customers on coupon orders were overcharged. Removed the `apply_tax()` call from the helper so it returns the post-discount subtotal only; callers own the tax step. Added `tests/test_issue_2.py`; full suite green (43 passed).
